   "text": "This SMILES was read region by region from the drawing. The stereochemistry is partly an estimate, because several wedge and hash bonds were hard to resolve at this resolution. The Asn, Thr, Trp and ring Lys centres are written as L-configured, the N-terminal Lys as D, and the Pen1, Pen2, Tyr and Nal centres follow my reading of the hashes. I could not check the SMILES with software.\n\n**Left side**\n- A (3R,S as drawn) 3-amino-4-trimethylammonio-butanoic acid (carnitine-like) unit.\n- Its amine is acylated by a dodecanedioyl chain (10 CH2 between the two C=O groups).\n- The chain's other end acylates the \u03b1-amine of Glu. The Glu \u03b3-carboxyl is joined to the linker, and its \u03b1-COOH is free.\n\n**Linker**\n- Glu \u03b3-C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013(CH2)4\u2013, ending on the Lys side chain.\n\n**Peptide**\n- Ac-Lys(linker) is the N-terminus.\n- The disulfide macrocycle contains Pen1, Asn, Thr, 7-methyl-Trp, Lys(Ac) and Pen2, with Pen1 and Pen2 joined through S\u2013S.\n- The tail after Pen2 is Tyr(O-CH2CH2NH2), 2-Nal, 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid, Lys(Ac), Asn, 3-pyridyl-Ala and Sar-NH2, ending in \u2013N(CH3)CH2C(=O)NH2.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@H](C[N+](C)(C)C)CC(=O)O)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@H]1C(C)(C)SSC(C)(C)[C@H](NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC1=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)C(=O)NC1(CCOCC1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1cccnc1)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O"
